Description: graphical console for SAS/SCSI/RAID HBAs and drive SMART
 A GTK3 graphical console for SAS, SCSI and RAID host bus adapters on
 Debian and Ubuntu based systems. It discovers every storage controller
 exposed through sysfs, resolves the controller model from the board name
 and the system pci.ids database (so Broadcom/LSI, Adaptec/Microchip,
 HPE, Intel, Marvell and others are shown correctly), lists the attached
 SAS/SATA drives, reads S.M.A.R.T. health data with smartctl, and can spin
 a single idle drive down or up or safely hot-remove it from the kernel.
 .
 The GUI itself runs unprivileged; privileged hardware access is provided by
 a minimal helper started on demand through pkexec and polkit.
